# Day 29 – Dynamic Portfolio with JavaScript

## What I Learned

Today I transformed my portfolio from a static website into a dynamic portfolio using JavaScript.

### Part 1 – Arrays of Objects

- Learned how to store multiple projects inside an array.
- Each project is represented as an object.
- Objects contain properties such as:
  - title
  - description
  - category
  - technologies
  - github
  - liveDemo

Example:

```javascript
const projects = [
    {
        title: "Portfolio",
        description: "Responsive portfolio website.",
        category: "HTML/CSS"
    }
];
```

### Part 2 – Dynamic Project Cards

Learned how to:

- createElement()
- appendChild()
- innerHTML
- forEach()

Instead of writing HTML manually, JavaScript creates project cards automatically.

### Part 3 – Project Filtering

Learned:

- filter()
- data attributes
- addEventListener()
- classList.add()
- classList.remove()

Built filter buttons that display only selected project categories.

### Part 4 – Project Modal

Learned how to:

- create a popup (modal)
- dynamically insert project information
- close the modal
- use multiple event listeners

### Part 5 – Portfolio Polish

Improved:

- project cards
- hover animations
- badges
- responsiveness
- modal styling

